[
  {
    "unit": 40,
    "page": 80,
    "width": 1490,
    "height": 2057,
    "title": "Agreement between subject and verb 1",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.024096188129194,
        "height": 2.034883712308866,
        "x": 1.606425753324962,
        "y": 1.889534867682774,
        "text": "Unit"
      },
      {
        "width": 5.823293084266201,
        "height": 2.761627842316472,
        "x": 1.606425736983366,
        "y": 4.505813979814965,
        "text": "40"
      },
      {
        "width": 57.63052101903313,
        "height": 2.784087011487424,
        "x": 12.449799725423192,
        "y": 4.9418604967000235,
        "text": "Agreement between subject and verb 1"
      },
      {
        "text": "A",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 8.9,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "width": 58.8353427144505,
        "height": 1.766503911440065,
        "x": 12.248995299188383,
        "y": 8.989310011565355,
        "text": "If a sentence has a singular subject, it is followed by a singular verb, and if it"
      },
      {
        "width": 16.064256501677853,
        "height": 1.184684866487229,
        "x": 75.30120507219003,
        "y": 9.135082585384957,
        "text": "Reminder → H1-H3"
      },
      {
        "width": 56.84138150823196,
        "height": 1.753333752542241,
        "x": 12.241487918321026,
        "y": 10.614745078119814,
        "text": "has a plural subject, it is followed by a plural verb; that is, the verb agrees"
      },
      {
        "width": 21.338226523175337,
        "height": 1.8020186873751953,
        "x": 12.222851246309451,
        "y": 12.309883855046944,
        "text": "with the subject. Compare:"
      },
      {
        "width": 68.47389579619339,
        "height": 1.60632351281228,
        "x": 15.863453698602603,
        "y": 14.091350862407948,
        "text": "• She lives in China. and • More people live in Asia than in any other continent."
      },
      {
        "width": 79.3172664770344,
        "height": 1.4577259475218707,
        "x": 12.248997273427213,
        "y": 16.569484917246,
        "text": "When the subject of the sentence is complex the following verb must agree with the main noun in the"
      },
      {
        "width": 77.52138278628354,
        "height": 1.6432496155200371,
        "x": 12.443698194662423,
        "y": 18.075312202430215,
        "text": "subject. In the examples below the subject is underlined and the main noun is circled. Note how the"
      },
      {
        "width": 33.13253108287017,
        "height": 1.612962439178367,
        "x": 12.248995487012033,
        "y": 19.912790739893026,
        "text": "verb, in italics, agrees with the main noun:"
      },
      {
        "width": 56.42570341993498,
        "height": 1.472274948950525,
        "x": 18.273092054830506,
        "y": 21.65697675361391,
        "text": "Many leading members of the opposition party have criticised the delay."
      },
      {
        "width": 51.030007176751255,
        "height": 1.907461702070612,
        "x": 18.463251079296462,
        "y": 23.075761159064978,
        "text": "The only excuse that he gave for his actions was that he was tired."
      },
      {
        "width": 72.48995582529363,
        "height": 1.6210138044737255,
        "x": 12.44980119456754,
        "y": 25.704567547526747,
        "text": "The verb must agree with the subject when the subject follows the verb (see Units 99 & 100):"
      },
      {
        "width": 75.5020039193582,
        "height": 1.4705799295557043,
        "x": 15.461849436011763,
        "y": 27.453838665200003,
        "text": "• Displayed on the board were the exam results. (compare The exam results were displayed …)"
      },
      {
        "width": 43.17268934825923,
        "height": 1.461257230204438,
        "x": 12.248996681243804,
        "y": 30.660835783002938,
        "text": "If the subject is a clause, we usually use a singular verb:"
      },
      {
        "width": 1.4056224951008014,
        "height": 1.3081394896215293,
        "x": 8.032128501445584,
        "y": 30.81395350165934,
        "text": "B"
      },
      {
        "width": 38.773189263055784,
        "height": 1.6957162536383907,
        "x": 18.464481186667136,
        "y": 32.262685046870175,
        "text": "To keep these young people in prison is inhuman."
      },
      {
        "width": 61.6465851444526,
        "height": 1.605052317775968,
        "x": 18.674699831388157,
        "y": 33.86627909688591,
        "text": "Having overall responsibility for the course means that I have a lot of meetings."
      },
      {
        "width": 32.12851505151531,
        "height": 1.4647885592268817,
        "x": 17.670682222510788,
        "y": 35.75581396266079,
        "text": "Whoever took them remains a mystery."
      },
      {
        "width": 76.50602814335151,
        "height": 1.6173412778982321,
        "x": 12.449797164173981,
        "y": 38.08139539170254,
        "text": "However, if we use a what-clause as subject (see Unit 98B), we use a singular verb if the following"
      },
      {
        "width": 73.09236872116192,
        "height": 1.476653787670379,
        "x": 12.248996352585106,
        "y": 39.825581404840825,
        "text": "main noun is singular, and either a singular or a plural verb if the following main noun is plural"
      },
      {
        "width": 47.616282213454284,
        "height": 1.8501537534307722,
        "x": 12.235153330225353,
        "y": 41.28674372213307,
        "text": "(although a plural verb is preferred in more formal contexts):"
      },
      {
        "width": 36.18123099307886,
        "height": 1.781846019570632,
        "x": 18.859041741040127,
        "y": 42.90588594231002,
        "text": "What worries us is the poor selection process."
      },
      {
        "width": 61.24497791264682,
        "height": 1.6140924830015058,
        "x": 18.67469980997891,
        "y": 44.75218654283495,
        "text": "What is needed are additional resources. (or more colloquially … needed is ...)"
      },
      {
        "width": 78.51406020606125,
        "height": 1.458997188898048,
        "x": 12.449797198511076,
        "y": 48.10495628953594,
        "text": "Some nouns with a singular form, referring to groups of some kind, can be used with either a singular"
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6064257269737716,
        "height": 1.3081394896215293,
        "x": 8.0321284919348,
        "y": 48.25581396521831,
        "text": "C"
      },
      {
        "width": 60.240961881291945,
        "height": 1.3119533527696903,
        "x": 12.650603385866422,
        "y": 49.854227407143604,
        "text": "or plural form of the verb. These nouns are sometimes called collective nouns:"
      },
      {
        "width": 53.01204809406459,
        "height": 1.3161909012567419,
        "x": 16.265060283319414,
        "y": 51.45348839439377,
        "text": "• The council has (or have) postponed a decision on the new road."
      },
      {
        "width": 76.50602814335151,
        "height": 1.3233948031945442,
        "x": 12.650600376141972,
        "y": 53.924418627109226,
        "text": "We use a singular verb if the focus is on the institution or organisation as a whole unit, and a plural"
      },
      {
        "width": 78.91566334154781,
        "height": 1.6196012728647569,
        "x": 12.248995633702968,
        "y": 55.52325585674184,
        "text": "verb if the focus is on a collection of individuals. Often you can use either with very little difference in"
      },
      {
        "width": 78.71486177380453,
        "height": 1.5988371230886367,
        "x": 12.449798019185296,
        "y": 57.26744190335413,
        "text": "meaning, although in formal contexts (such as academic writing) it is common to use a singular verb."
      },
      {
        "width": 72.69076558567534,
        "height": 1.6143749707873578,
        "x": 13.45381398659891,
        "y": 61.321671497444065,
        "text": "Also: army, association, audience, class, club, college, commission, committee, community,"
      },
      {
        "width": 69.08708610790688,
        "height": 1.822366705209566,
        "x": 13.648473232594199,
        "y": 62.877050451889225,
        "text": "company, crew, crowd, department, electorate, enemy, family, federation, generation,"
      },
      {
        "width": 76.90763127883808,
        "height": 1.6046284934174482,
        "x": 13.654618096346805,
        "y": 64.6744412304116,
        "text": "government, group, institute, jury, opposition, orchestra, population, press, public, school, team,"
      },
      {
        "width": 74.71609230809563,
        "height": 1.9690397761190193,
        "x": 13.646556088075323,
        "y": 66.18847590199405,
        "text": "university; the Bank of England, the BBC, IBM, Sony, the United Nations (specific organisations)"
      },
      {
        "width": 55.220881724517625,
        "height": 1.318450942563132,
        "x": 12.650603307693736,
        "y": 68.895348859444,
        "text": "In some contexts we have to use a singular or a plural form of the verb."
      },
      {
        "width": 36.94779159238674,
        "height": 1.6176237656840842,
        "x": 13.654618244585132,
        "y": 71.51162794940032,
        "text": "• The committee usually raise their hands to"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.939759529677005,
        "height": 1.4769362754562199,
        "x": 16.666666408976756,
        "y": 73.25581396260601,
        "text": "vote 'Yes'. (not The committee usually raises"
      },
      {
        "width": 9.839357721725566,
        "height": 1.4534883526949427,
        "x": 16.66666651041399,
        "y": 75.00000000818498,
        "text": "its hands ...)"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.33734868196833,
        "height": 1.3260785761797123,
        "x": 53.41365496593865,
        "y": 71.51162792920901,
        "text": "This is something the individuals do, not the"
      },
      {
        "width": 18.106591141463934,
        "height": 1.462370730697582,
        "x": 53.39893668329081,
        "y": 73.10873732020002,
        "text": "committee as a whole."
      },
      {
        "width": 31.726907819709517,
        "height": 1.6159287462892524,
        "x": 16.867469774556085,
        "y": 77.45383865194187,
        "text": "The school is to close next year. (not The"
      },
      {
        "width": 17.26907614893561,
        "height": 1.611267327103838,
        "x": 16.66666693557235,
        "y": 79.05733726096663,
        "text": "school are to close ...)"
      },
      {
        "width": 32.158168306286704,
        "height": 1.8022065491671735,
        "x": 53.198056667826,
        "y": 77.22619138856992,
        "text": "This is something that will happen to the"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.53815229787123,
        "height": 1.3205697399765959,
        "x": 53.413654764656634,
        "y": 79.05733721373024,
        "text": "school as a building or institution, not to the"
      },
      {
        "width": 19.879519059354024,
        "height": 1.3154846354522576,
        "x": 53.01204768898712,
        "y": 80.80660836448396,
        "text": "individuals in the school."
      },
      {
        "width": 75.3121067533557,
        "height": 1.6528084164574075,
        "x": 12.845881336981785,
        "y": 84.5532827644448,
        "text": "When names and titles ending in -s refer to a single unit we use a singular verb. Examples include"
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6064257269737716,
        "height": 1.3081394896215293,
        "x": 8.0321284919348,
        "y": 84.88372094196248,
        "text": "D"
      },
      {
        "width": 66.26506216574035,
        "height": 1.4664835786217023,
        "x": 12.650601442150547,
        "y": 86.33720931164011,
        "text": "countries; newspapers; titles of books, films, etc.; and quoted plural words or phrases:"
      },
      {
        "width": 54.02409291107383,
        "height": 1.5264538912314385,
        "x": 18.26873136042987,
        "y": 87.91448057347412,
        "text": "At this time of the year the Netherlands is one hour ahead of the UK."
      },
      {
        "width": 57.22891378722734,
        "height": 1.184684866487229,
        "x": 18.674699724009077,
        "y": 89.68023254712357,
        "text": "The Machine Gunners was one of Robert Westall's most successful books."
      },
      {
        "width": 58.04185291264681,
        "height": 1.8015102464325583,
        "x": 18.067788623722844,
        "y": 91.23606714648821,
        "text": "'Daps' is the word used in the south-west of the country for sports shoes."
      },
      {
        "width": 2.811244990201605,
        "height": 1.3081394896215293,
        "x": 3.413654603292773,
        "y": 97.23837211020377,
        "text": "80"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "unit": 41,
    "page": 82,
    "width": 1490,
    "height": 2059,
    "title": "Agreement between subject and verb 2",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.2248992919921875,
        "height": 2.03488377691472,
        "x": 2.8112450992348297,
        "y": 2.0348836802199677,
        "text": "Unit"
      },
      {
        "width": 5.220883260637323,
        "height": 2.616279009476452,
        "x": 3.212851532331941,
        "y": 4.651162814897081,
        "text": "41"
      },
      {
        "width": 57.83132668309563,
        "height": 2.776586106679968,
        "x": 13.85542098965679,
        "y": 4.941860485894233,
        "text": "Agreement between subject and verb 2"
      },
      {
        "text": "A",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 9,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "width": 36.14457712877518,
        "height": 1.4749378833955884,
        "x": 14.658635119690047,
        "y": 9.593023261838528,
        "text": "With any of, each of, either of, neither of, or"
      },
      {
        "width": 35.3413667614828,
        "height": 1.453488359173516,
        "x": 14.859437078832741,
        "y": 11.191860470204817,
        "text": "none of and a plural noun / pronoun we can"
      },
      {
        "width": 36.54618436058096,
        "height": 1.4769135169612535,
        "x": 14.658634718445404,
        "y": 12.912621359812182,
        "text": "use a singular or plural verb. (We use a singular"
      },
      {
        "width": 25.100400783871645,
        "height": 1.619157791137693,
        "x": 14.658634940694704,
        "y": 14.5145631404487,
        "text": "verb for careful written English.)"
      },
      {
        "width": 35.94377556103188,
        "height": 1.6202867378309005,
        "x": 54.216867229524226,
        "y": 9.4476744157312,
        "text": "• I don't think any of them knows (or know)"
      },
      {
        "width": 22.088352689807056,
        "height": 1.598837213608828,
        "x": 57.22891601716012,
        "y": 11.19186046173315,
        "text": "where the money is hidden."
      },
      {
        "width": 37.951807623741615,
        "height": 1.622544538627546,
        "x": 54.01606379426804,
        "y": 12.766990335826367,
        "text": "• Neither of the French athletes has (or have)"
      },
      {
        "width": 11.504852499737828,
        "height": 1.4555895907207628,
        "x": 57.206212369087254,
        "y": 14.643069584263134,
        "text": "won this year."
      },
      {
        "width": 35.140561097420296,
        "height": 1.4687288154676015,
        "x": 14.658635103349308,
        "y": 17.13592234042021,
        "text": "With a / the majority of, a number of, a lot"
      },
      {
        "width": 37.7510019596791,
        "height": 1.6109731359389312,
        "x": 14.658635555570381,
        "y": 18.737864075029197,
        "text": "of, plenty of, all (of), or some (of) and a plural"
      },
      {
        "width": 37.14859316013003,
        "height": 1.4622375340137772,
        "x": 14.859438349351903,
        "y": 20.485436877584707,
        "text": "noun / pronoun we use a plural verb. (We use a"
      },
      {
        "width": 27.309236462484265,
        "height": 1.6044817618953378,
        "x": 14.658635076990786,
        "y": 22.087378685388725,
        "text": "singular verb with the number of.)"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.136547114225046,
        "height": 1.3233799610323116,
        "x": 54.61847342085853,
        "y": 17.135922349089316,
        "text": "• A number of refugees have been turned"
      },
      {
        "width": 15.10286164763791,
        "height": 1.4239118631603653,
        "x": 57.21150648652061,
        "y": 18.642651907820216,
        "text": "back at the border."
      },
      {
        "width": 34.13654506606544,
        "height": 1.7534996699360983,
        "x": 54.01606448704762,
        "y": 20.194174741992942,
        "text": "• The number of books in the library has"
      },
      {
        "width": 19.747336982880668,
        "height": 1.8828066112925645,
        "x": 57.20276223121081,
        "y": 21.824776588879892,
        "text": "risen to over five million."
      },
      {
        "width": 35.54216832922609,
        "height": 1.3106796116504782,
        "x": 14.8594379097957,
        "y": 24.708737866788443,
        "text": "After one of and a plural noun / pronoun we"
      },
      {
        "width": 33.935743498322154,
        "height": 1.4588507402290452,
        "x": 14.85943748061517,
        "y": 26.308139540732768,
        "text": "use a singular verb. However, after one of +"
      },
      {
        "width": 37.19832657167575,
        "height": 1.8965607244991523,
        "x": 14.829718426939548,
        "y": 27.618847033186643,
        "text": "plural noun / pronoun + who we can often use"
      },
      {
        "width": 36.345382792837675,
        "height": 1.61097313593892,
        "x": 14.658633894688124,
        "y": 29.651162788084996,
        "text": "either a singular or plural verb. (A plural verb is"
      },
      {
        "width": 15.926085606517407,
        "height": 1.7410578311068403,
        "x": 14.631486075239316,
        "y": 31.33272931208054,
        "text": "more grammatical.)"
      },
      {
        "width": 36.96524600854656,
        "height": 1.5559140918324221,
        "x": 54.40890059725119,
        "y": 24.516923073379935,
        "text": "• One of the reasons I took the job was that I"
      },
      {
        "width": 18.71149459941275,
        "height": 1.5835497217270844,
        "x": 57.41337062279961,
        "y": 26.18819780393309,
        "text": "could work from home."
      },
      {
        "width": 33.33333265061347,
        "height": 1.6073041749231964,
        "x": 54.21686775386709,
        "y": 27.76162790196843,
        "text": "• He's one of those teachers who insist /"
      },
      {
        "width": 30.321284556548868,
        "height": 1.6109731359389312,
        "x": 57.22891594921382,
        "y": 29.651162787581264,
        "text": "insists on pupils sitting silently in class."
      },
      {
        "width": 32.3293166192586,
        "height": 1.619157791137693,
        "x": 14.658634852482233,
        "y": 33.86627906707768,
        "text": "With any of, none of, the majority of, a"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.17153377660969,
        "height": 1.9478475700304365,
        "x": 14.639005855212545,
        "y": 35.30924172969445,
        "text": "lot of, plenty of, all (of), some (of) and an"
      },
      {
        "width": 33.33333265061347,
        "height": 1.598837213608828,
        "x": 14.658634872435059,
        "y": 37.209302322772885,
        "text": "uncountable noun we use a singular verb."
      },
      {
        "width": 35.763422818791945,
        "height": 1.657317263408764,
        "x": 54.20771385257066,
        "y": 33.71363456937024,
        "text": "• All the furniture was destroyed in the fire."
      },
      {
        "width": 32.931727466967274,
        "height": 1.6222623251016755,
        "x": 54.21686717991353,
        "y": 35.465116276404075,
        "text": "• None of the equipment appears to be"
      },
      {
        "width": 8.260583045498638,
        "height": 1.5375974340346321,
        "x": 57.41589320537018,
        "y": 37.16724779248075,
        "text": "damaged."
      },
      {
        "width": 33.93574349832215,
        "height": 1.4735267694713894,
        "x": 14.859437474426826,
        "y": 39.66019415371533,
        "text": "With every or each and a singular noun or"
      },
      {
        "width": 35.742969896969385,
        "height": 1.4701399756866684,
        "x": 14.65863552420607,
        "y": 41.407766994113274,
        "text": "coordinated noun (x and y) we use a singular"
      },
      {
        "width": 23.694779568870594,
        "height": 1.757733150593288,
        "x": 14.658634316484509,
        "y": 43.00970871782488,
        "text": "verb. (For each of, see above.)"
      },
      {
        "width": 30.722891788354655,
        "height": 1.3281779150360995,
        "x": 54.41767056060476,
        "y": 39.66019416242991,
        "text": "• Every room looks over the harbour."
      },
      {
        "width": 37.349398824192534,
        "height": 1.6157710436478512,
        "x": 54.216866842512815,
        "y": 41.262135934782094,
        "text": "• Every boy and girl takes part in the activity."
      },
      {
        "width": 30.722891788354655,
        "height": 1.467035441722686,
        "x": 54.216867348224895,
        "y": 43.00970873734866,
        "text": "• Each child has drawn a picture. but"
      },
      {
        "width": 34.53815229787123,
        "height": 1.6092797621940047,
        "x": 54.21686792234952,
        "y": 44.611650452531926,
        "text": "• The children have each drawn a picture."
      },
      {
        "width": 35.74296989696937,
        "height": 1.604199640959214,
        "x": 14.658635533217398,
        "y": 47.23300966262139,
        "text": "With everyone, everybody, everything (and"
      },
      {
        "width": 35.94377556103188,
        "height": 1.3106796116504893,
        "x": 14.859437510878212,
        "y": 48.980582520668214,
        "text": "similar words beginning any-, some- and no-)"
      },
      {
        "width": 17.922942910418417,
        "height": 1.7823797985188072,
        "x": 14.829605603588172,
        "y": 50.45238505118116,
        "text": "we use a singular verb."
      },
      {
        "width": 37.16704707817744,
        "height": 1.6694611484564637,
        "x": 54.20900451092907,
        "y": 47.088967938900915,
        "text": "• Practically everyone thinks that Phil should"
      },
      {
        "width": 13.453815639419043,
        "height": 1.4563106796116498,
        "x": 57.429718675636956,
        "y": 48.98058251127541,
        "text": "be given the job."
      },
      {
        "width": 63.453815639419055,
        "height": 1.465059808157021,
        "x": 14.056224713216297,
        "y": 54.50581395941375,
        "text": "When a subject has two or more items joined by and, we usually use a plural verb:"
      },
      {
        "width": 1.4056224951008027,
        "height": 1.308139504738226,
        "x": 9.437750991405421,
        "y": 54.796511633635866,
        "text": "B"
      },
      {
        "width": 40.76305415006291,
        "height": 1.6140776699029136,
        "x": 16.666665685646674,
        "y": 56.249999997430386,
        "text": "• Ingrid and Tobias are moving back to Australia."
      },
      {
        "width": 75.11370562867029,
        "height": 1.835881668387107,
        "x": 13.849037726660162,
        "y": 58.505796384203045,
        "text": "However, phrases connected by and can also be followed by singular verbs if we think of them as"
      },
      {
        "width": 19.277108211645345,
        "height": 1.476631303435394,
        "x": 13.65461857445066,
        "y": 60.46511628444482,
        "text": "making up a single item:"
      },
      {
        "width": 64.67064774276426,
        "height": 1.817923981009184,
        "x": 16.86308596711436,
        "y": 61.90837852921396,
        "text": "• The lorry, its cargo and passengers weighs around 35 tonnes. (or ... weigh ...)"
      },
      {
        "width": 78.91566334154783,
        "height": 1.6177466309186372,
        "x": 13.654618120925639,
        "y": 65.24271848716461,
        "text": "When a subject is made up of two or more items joined by (either) ... or ... or (neither) ... nor ... we"
      },
      {
        "text": "C",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 65.7,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "width": 76.30521838296981,
        "height": 1.6146420969546327,
        "x": 13.654619722322495,
        "y": 66.84466023034554,
        "text": "use a singular verb if the last item is singular (although a plural verb is sometimes used in informal"
      },
      {
        "width": 38.95582365509647,
        "height": 1.7566042039000918,
        "x": 13.654618284259943,
        "y": 68.59223301565245,
        "text": "English), and a plural verb if the last item is plural:"
      },
      {
        "width": 70.69623499108641,
        "height": 1.9237488681830284,
        "x": 20.0749562273903,
        "y": 70.12210040124545,
        "text": "Either the station or the cinema is a good place to meet. (or ... are ... in informal English)"
      },
      {
        "width": 50.60240879954908,
        "height": 1.4594152135756322,
        "x": 20.281125268900148,
        "y": 71.94174755249368,
        "text": "The President or his representatives are to attend the meeting."
      },
      {
        "width": 67.46987976483851,
        "height": 1.6019417475728215,
        "x": 13.654618343078152,
        "y": 74.41747570201122,
        "text": "If the last item is singular and previous item plural, we can use a singular or plural verb:"
      },
      {
        "width": 71.48593979393875,
        "height": 1.458286266882447,
        "x": 17.269078317049484,
        "y": 76.01744186607982,
        "text": "• Either the teachers or the principal is to blame for the accident. (or ... are to blame ...)"
      },
      {
        "width": 77.30923441432466,
        "height": 1.3191465266699898,
        "x": 13.654619731394574,
        "y": 79.36046513113307,
        "text": "In there + be / have (see Unit 95) we use a singular verb form with singular and uncountable nouns"
      },
      {
        "text": "D",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 80.1,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "width": 77.11882111210151,
        "height": 1.6470862823782628,
        "x": 13.850795921287212,
        "y": 80.89589279981098,
        "text": "and a plural form with plural nouns. However, in informal speech we often use a shortened singular"
      },
      {
        "width": 38.59834197383599,
        "height": 1.930923554503794,
        "x": 13.83448228634642,
        "y": 82.4180204193591,
        "text": "form of be or have (= There's) with plural nouns:"
      },
      {
        "width": 59.046176167942534,
        "height": 1.61573984090565,
        "x": 20.07560985316693,
        "y": 84.2663556934869,
        "text": "Over the last few years there have been many improvements in car safety."
      },
      {
        "width": 49.19678553638843,
        "height": 1.598837213608817,
        "x": 19.879518869452266,
        "y": 86.04651162538869,
        "text": "There's been lots of good films on lately. (or There’ve been …)"
      },
      {
        "width": 2.811244990201605,
        "height": 1.453488359173527,
        "x": 4.819277103292772,
        "y": 97.09302324773881,
        "text": "82"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "unit": 42,
    "page": 84,
    "width": 1488,
    "height": 2058,
    "title": "Agreement between subject and verb 3",
    "lines": [
      {
        "text": "Unit",
        "y": 1.7441860338649473,
        "width": 6.024096089024697,
        "height": 2.034883712308866,
        "x": 2.8112450880177717
      },
      {
        "text": "42",
        "y": 4.215116304824596,
        "width": 5.622489990726594,
        "height": 2.761627842316472,
        "x": 2.8112449549140033
      },
      {
        "text": "Agreement between subject and verb 3",
        "y": 4.47606554958544,
        "width": 57.866324147870465,
        "height": 3.0978025801559506,
        "x": 13.638269044579468
      },
      {
        "text": "A",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 8.2,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "text": "Plural nouns",
        "y": 8.843537433838911,
        "width": 11.445782774238175,
        "height": 1.1855322835049198,
        "x": 13.65461862543111
      },
      {
        "text": "Some nouns are usually plural and take a",
        "y": 11.467444138380811,
        "width": 31.726906889228413,
        "height": 1.3232535129617529,
        "x": 13.654618833750956
      },
      {
        "text": "Also: belongings, clothes, congratulations, goods,",
        "y": 12.34207966485289,
        "width": 40.96385586646296,
        "height": 1.6114086636764724,
        "x": 48.393574065506336
      },
      {
        "text": "plural verb:",
        "y": 13.201696526422268,
        "width": 9.05134036976804,
        "height": 1.5035836875033182,
        "x": 13.446217355296653
      },
      {
        "text": "outskirts, overheads, particulars",
        "y": 14.091350861916851,
        "width": 26.907629607826145,
        "height": 1.60632351281228,
        "x": 48.39357474485894
      },
      {
        "text": "• The company's earnings have",
        "y": 14.820213778766034,
        "width": 26.305221229471186,
        "height": 1.3135071282715738,
        "x": 16.867469695384198
      },
      {
        "text": "(= information), premises (= building), riches, savings,",
        "y": 15.694849398068323,
        "width": 43.57429832540532,
        "height": 1.603498542274051,
        "x": 48.192770505598205
      },
      {
        "text": "increased for the last five years.",
        "y": 16.160990266014185,
        "width": 24.962769785235007,
        "height": 1.9370940035123962,
        "x": 19.453152364441248
      },
      {
        "text": "stairs, surroundings, thanks",
        "y": 17.44186050739899,
        "width": 23.092370392173844,
        "height": 1.6057585372405758,
        "x": 48.39357383084555
      },
      {
        "text": "Note that whereabouts can be used with either a singular or plural verb, police and people always",
        "y": 20.348837252123666,
        "width": 77.30923724430863,
        "height": 1.6142337268944318,
        "x": 13.453815104072014
      },
      {
        "text": "take a plural verb, and staff usually does:",
        "y": 22.09302329832864,
        "width": 32.530120111280866,
        "height": 1.6193187850789048,
        "x": 13.253012222955432
      },
      {
        "text": "• Police believe that Thomas is in Brazil, although his exact whereabouts are / is unknown.",
        "y": 23.624789416691726,
        "width": 72.69917970062583,
        "height": 1.635887880019471,
        "x": 16.661778335785186
      },
      {
        "text": "Staff say that the new computer system has led to greater levels of stress in their work.",
        "y": 25.413022317064126,
        "width": 69.47790986748153,
        "height": 1.62186136051099,
        "x": 18.674699675191864
      },
      {
        "text": "Plural nouns used with singular verbs",
        "y": 28.32993767084755,
        "width": 34.58900041477654,
        "height": 2.1890744060075074,
        "x": 13.428611299179838
      },
      {
        "text": "B",
        "y": 28.779069745037244,
        "width": 1.2048191921685338,
        "height": 1.1627907192278353,
        "x": 9.437751034437824
      },
      {
        "text": "Although the words data and media (= newspaper, television, etc.) are plural (singular datum",
        "y": 31.092432338802432,
        "width": 72.90176063455561,
        "height": 1.7498539071041264,
        "x": 13.448980498260617
      },
      {
        "text": "and medium), they are commonly used with a singular verb. However, in formal contexts such",
        "y": 32.847424720545604,
        "width": 73.49397392683132,
        "height": 1.6034985422740622,
        "x": 13.453816240994332
      },
      {
        "text": "as academic writing a plural verb is preferred. Note that other similar plurals such as criteria and",
        "y": 34.44767446145771,
        "width": 75.30120521463373,
        "height": 1.6067473371707774,
        "x": 13.453815055174372
      },
      {
        "text": "phenomena (singular criterion and phenomenon) are always used with plural verbs. Compare:",
        "y": 36.19186047445555,
        "width": 74.49799404349378,
        "height": 1.4660598469429242,
        "x": 13.654617431064347
      },
      {
        "text": "• All the data is available for public inspection. (or ... are available ...) and",
        "y": 37.936046521037404,
        "width": 59.03614413353705,
        "height": 1.4711449051274084,
        "x": 17.068273306437455
      },
      {
        "text": "I agree that the criteria are not of equal importance. (not ... the criteria is not ...)",
        "y": 39.457981033830094,
        "width": 64.27196379630796,
        "height": 1.79990484832675,
        "x": 18.869653758865727
      },
      {
        "text": "Uncountable nouns ending in -s",
        "y": 42.85714286910001,
        "width": 28.915661637501046,
        "height": 1.6196012728647569,
        "x": 13.65461897383445
      },
      {
        "text": "C",
        "x": 8,
        "y": 43.2,
        "width": 1.3,
        "height": 1.2
      },
      {
        "text": "Some uncountable nouns always end in -s",
        "y": 45.33080861592338,
        "width": 32.95077252131636,
        "height": 1.5947862778970423,
        "x": 13.646289396055137
      },
      {
        "text": "Also: means (='method' or 'money'); economics,",
        "y": 46.06413994018263,
        "width": 39.15662457866054,
        "height": 1.6102786198533559,
        "x": 53.0120491418662
      },
      {
        "text": "and look as if they are plural, but when we use",
        "y": 47.084548108652015,
        "width": 36.144576534148186,
        "height": 1.6073123127424926,
        "x": 13.453816138393934
      },
      {
        "text": "linguistics, mathematics, phonetics, physics;",
        "y": 47.959183707490084,
        "width": 37.14859254898564,
        "height": 1.6047697373103853,
        "x": 53.01204909635102
      },
      {
        "text": "them as the subject they have a singular verb:",
        "y": 48.83381923943784,
        "width": 35.74297094857821,
        "height": 1.3119533527696903,
        "x": 13.654618933341414
      },
      {
        "text": "politics, statistics; athletics, gymnastics;",
        "y": 49.70845482508863,
        "width": 33.73493891890331,
        "height": 1.4577259475218596,
        "x": 53.21285181544385
      },
      {
        "text": "The news from the Middle East seems",
        "y": 50.436046500008594,
        "width": 30.120482496035994,
        "height": 1.1674520457335413,
        "x": 19.477911353111157
      },
      {
        "text": "diabetes, measles, rabies",
        "y": 51.30813957711209,
        "width": 21.084336311586448,
        "height": 1.6073123127424704,
        "x": 53.01204870097451
      },
      {
        "text": "very encouraging.",
        "y": 52.18023254966998,
        "width": 14.257028025965537,
        "height": 1.4640823397622516,
        "x": 19.87951820840277
      },
      {
        "text": "However, compare:",
        "y": 54.63852644330635,
        "width": 15.300424637333041,
        "height": 1.5544265769313448,
        "x": 13.827697901273748
      },
      {
        "text": "academic subject",
        "y": 57.26744186686077,
        "width": 13.654618622154317,
        "height": 1.4534883526949427,
        "x": 14.658634460372275
      },
      {
        "text": "general use",
        "y": 57.28636120985971,
        "width": 8.910089923489483,
        "height": 1.170319741622583,
        "x": 54.371605488201865
      },
      {
        "text": "Her politics are bordering on the fascist.",
        "y": 59.56151151571579,
        "width": 31.94575771208732,
        "height": 1.601020657286345,
        "x": 57.21956673651394
      },
      {
        "text": "• Politics is popular at this university.",
        "y": 59.718172974353045,
        "width": 31.32530130365844,
        "height": 1.4736874805595046,
        "x": 14.658634478135085
      },
      {
        "text": "(= political belief)",
        "y": 61.32167150959701,
        "width": 14.056225233180541,
        "height": 1.4690261540537985,
        "x": 57.429718698670776
      },
      {
        "text": "Statistics are able to prove anything you",
        "y": 63.7998056316194,
        "width": 32.32931731849589,
        "height": 1.6071710688495555,
        "x": 57.22891562590795
      },
      {
        "text": "• Statistics was always my worst subject.",
        "y": 63.94557821357165,
        "width": 34.53815419186829,
        "height": 1.4613985204372293,
        "x": 14.85943694906163
      },
      {
        "text": "want them to. (= numerical information)",
        "y": 65.34491912162946,
        "width": 32.15953252648794,
        "height": 1.7398846276879265,
        "x": 57.41432244202802
      },
      {
        "text": "• Economics has only recently been",
        "y": 68.0129018343275,
        "width": 30.144738638272848,
        "height": 1.6795357647627962,
        "x": 14.64697419561429
      },
      {
        "text": "• The economics behind their policies are",
        "y": 68.02325582316148,
        "width": 34.738954933740764,
        "height": 1.4616810082230813,
        "x": 54.216867903190945
      },
      {
        "text": "unreasonable. (= the financial system)",
        "y": 69.6220930651695,
        "width": 29.919677652338507,
        "height": 1.6121148831411136,
        "x": 57.429719409010275
      },
      {
        "text": "recognised as a scientific study.",
        "y": 69.62362039977735,
        "width": 24.730811580534905,
        "height": 1.7763934862972786,
        "x": 17.85369582171052
      },
      {
        "text": "Agrement with measurements, percentages, etc.",
        "y": 73.57177977789682,
        "width": 44.19216853316112,
        "height": 1.8734343429580247,
        "x": 13.846229856242035
      },
      {
        "text": "D",
        "y": 73.83720931405551,
        "width": 1.6064256750127321,
        "height": 1.3081394896215404,
        "x": 9.236947795023756
      },
      {
        "text": "With a phrase referring to a measurement, amount or quantity we usually prefer a singular verb:",
        "y": 76.14188534625262,
        "width": 74.69879478536625,
        "height": 1.6197425167576829,
        "x": 13.654618691006467
      },
      {
        "text": "• Only three metres separates the runners in first and second places. (rather than … separate …)",
        "y": 77.75857433177521,
        "width": 75.11588476037467,
        "height": 1.8095230569644905,
        "x": 17.061967684863568
      },
      {
        "text": "and a singular verb must be used when the complement is a singular noun phrase (e.g. a long time):",
        "y": 79.49465499944726,
        "width": 77.30923724430863,
        "height": 1.4646473153339556,
        "x": 13.855421576062788
      },
      {
        "text": "Three hours seems a long time to take on the homework. (not Three hours seem ...)",
        "y": 81.13145551193762,
        "width": 66.67984993227066,
        "height": 1.6597039729675411,
        "x": 18.871035548972078
      },
      {
        "text": "When the first noun in a complex subject is a percentage or a fraction the verb agrees with the noun",
        "y": 83.5755814377355,
        "width": 77.51003798618112,
        "height": 1.6042047617386812,
        "x": 13.855422781937477
      },
      {
        "text": "closest to the verb. Compare:",
        "y": 85.33149893263557,
        "width": 22.722100698819723,
        "height": 1.4734571251160178,
        "x": 14.040211018769892
      },
      {
        "text": "An inflation rate of only 2% makes a difference to exports. (verb agrees with main noun) and",
        "y": 86.72637701901057,
        "width": 73.10970675560738,
        "height": 1.7488385080943636,
        "x": 19.67224117224759
      },
      {
        "text": "About 50% / half of the houses need major repairs. (verb agrees with closest noun)",
        "y": 88.66279070711015,
        "width": 65.46184580813173,
        "height": 1.4732637025408613,
        "x": 19.678715641929717
      },
      {
        "text": "Where we use a singular noun that can be thought of as either a whole unit or a collection of",
        "y": 90.95181928622402,
        "width": 72.10511238344253,
        "height": 1.7066731281484393,
        "x": 14.04862805283095
      },
      {
        "text": "individuals, we can use either a singular or plural verb:",
        "y": 92.85714284921441,
        "width": 42.16867262317288,
        "height": 1.3289036393976494,
        "x": 13.855422716407888
      },
      {
        "text": "Some 80% of the electorate is expected to vote. (or ... are expected ...)",
        "y": 94.3183171498416,
        "width": 58.04410954957366,
        "height": 1.6401448449078315,
        "x": 18.669234621669112
      },
